Bundled fonts - excalidraw-assets/*.woff2
================================================================================

Virgil.woff2
  Copyright (c) 2020 Excalidraw
  MIT License (see the Excalidraw section above).

Assistant-Regular.woff2, Assistant-Medium.woff2, Assistant-SemiBold.woff2,
Assistant-Bold.woff2
  Copyright (c) 2016 The Assistant Project Authors
  https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Assistant
  SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The complete license text is included in
  `../../../licenses/OFL-1.1.txt` and in `THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md`.

Cascadia.woff2
  Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation
  https://github.com/microsoft/cascadia-code
  SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The complete license text is included in
  `../../../licenses/OFL-1.1.txt` and in `THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md`.

Upstream Excalidraw ships these font binaries inside its build output without
per-font license files. The attributions above trace each face back to its
original foundry so the OFL notice requirement travels with our copies.

================================================================================
Note on the upstream webpack notice file
================================================================================

excalidraw.js begins with a banner pointing at
"excalidraw-with-preact.production.min.js.LICENSE.txt", the file webpack uses to
collect notices for the libraries compiled into that bundle. That upstream file
is included beside the bundle as
`excalidraw-with-preact.production.min.js.LICENSE.txt`.
